# Toss relay allow-list. Copy to /etc/toss-relay/allowed.txt
#
# One endpoint id per line: 64 lowercase hex characters. Text after # is ignored.
# No ids at all (or file missing) = relay is OPEN: anyone who knows the URL can
# use it (rate limits in relay.toml still apply).
# With at least one id = ONLY these devices may use the relay. Add the studio
# host AND every editor, otherwise that editor silently falls back to n0's relay.
#
# Get a full id on a device:  toss-cli id        (first column)
# (The Toss app only shows a shortened id.)
#
# After editing run:  sudo /opt/toss-relay/update-allowed.sh
#
# 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef  # may tong
